Chapter: InductionListUnsound

 Stage 5 soundness tripwire for N-ary constructor congruence. The MyCons
 case of `append xs MyNil === xs` normalizes to
 `MyCons h (append t MyNil) === MyCons h t`, which holds only via the
 inductive hypothesis (`cong ih`), NOT by reflexivity. Offering `Refl`
 asserts `append t MyNil` and `t` are definitionally equal, which they
 are not. If the curried-constructor peel in the unifier were unsound
 (collapsing the two arguments), this would be wrongly accepted; it must
 reject with CDX2001.

Section: List

  MyList =
   | MyNil
   | MyCons (Integer) (MyList)

  append : MyList, MyList -> MyList
  append (xs) (ys) = when xs
   is MyNil -> ys
   is MyCons (h) (t) -> MyCons h (append t ys)

Section: Bad Proof

  claim append-nil-bad : for all (xs : MyList), append xs MyNil === xs
  proof append-nil-bad =
   induction on xs
    is MyNil -> Refl
    is MyCons (h) (t) (ih) -> Refl
   qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "unreachable"
  end
